{
  "schema": "delve.audio.sounds.v1",
  "description": "Maps run cues, monsters and floor themes to donor sound file names under the gitignored content import area (delve/imports/audio, staged by scripts/extract-delver-reference.sh from the operator's donor jar audio/). Names follow the donor: weapon swings (entities/items/Sword.java swingSound), monster hits and swipes (entities/Monster.java hitSound, attackSwingSound), doors (entities/Door.java), pickups (entities/Item.java, items/Gold.java), monster alert/attack/hurt/die sets (data/monsters.dat; our monsters borrow the donor set named in 'donor'), and each section's music and ambient sound (generator/<Section>/section.dat music, ambientSound 0.15). A cue picks one of its files at random. 'world' cues play where they happened; the rest play at the listener. The sound data is donor-derived and never committed; without it the game is silent.",
